{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1177776-are-rank-6-cryptids-made-from-ephemera","id":1177776,"title":"Are Rank 6+ Cryptids made from Ephemera?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-20T22:47:54-08:00","id":1177776,"title":"Are Rank 6+ Cryptids made from Ephemera?","content":"&quot;Cryptids with Rank 6 are exceedingly rare, one-of-akind<br /> monsters that only occur when a resident of a different<br /> supernatural world, like the Hedge or the Shadow, encounters<br /> the God-Machine. These beings are so alien that they cannot<br /> survive long in this world, living swift and violent lives before<br /> fleeing to realms that better suit them.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the case of the Hedge I assume this means some sort of animal like Hedge denizen, but I don't know of any actual animals coming from the Shadow. Should I take this to mean that rank 6+ cryptids are or can be made from ephemera, or is there another interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T00:04:41-08:00","id":1177791,"title":"","content":"Seems legit. Although I wonder if this could mean that a comparatively weak spirit could end up noticeably more powerful as a Cryptid. Rank 1 spirit turning into Rank 6 Cryptid, anyone? (Yeah, I know ephemeral Rank and Cryptid Rank aren't the same, but still!)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Mage 1E had mentions of its own Cryptids. They were some weird half-spirit, half-flesh creatures skittering around Shadow Verges. Sorta like Pangaeans from Dark Eras, only much lesser. Maybe they could be the 'animals' of the Shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T08:07:43-08:00","id":1177849,"title":"","content":"I'd say the reason there are no Rank 6+ Cryptids in the &quot; normal&quot; world is that they would make big waves and the God-Machine would crack down on them hard. For them to survive, they would have to go to a realm the G-M has less oversight on.<br /> <br /> But since material beings can still exist in the Ephemeral Realms, I don't see why 6+ Cryptids <i>have</i> to be Ephemeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T09:02:06-08:00","id":1177858,"title":"","content":"I suspect such rare and weird things are hard to categorise or quantify<br /> <br /> A cryptid-spirit and cryptid-goblin are really quite different; I'd go ephemeral for the former, material for the latter. Cryptid-ghosts pretty much already exist and use the ghost rules (with some angelic numina and demonic abilities) and I'd do much the same for spirits (so probably a lower rank than 6 average). Hedge-cryptids... use the normal cryptid rules but maybe throw some weird fae powers in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 01-21-2018, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T11:48:13-08:00","id":1177902,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say that, barring plot related intervention by the Storyteller, the state of a cryptid would depend on their natural state. An ephemeral being would remain ephemeral, and a material being would remain material. I agree with Eremite that a hobgoblin would be material, and have been working on and off on a Rank 6 cryptid that uses a hobgoblin as a base creature. She is definitely physical, living her life as best she can and pretending to be an ordinary mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 01-22-2018, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}